        <h2 class="section-title">It started as a notebook <em>in a nightstand.</em></h2>
        <p>There was a season where I was being made to feel like I wasn't offering enough of myself. The comments landed wrong. And like most women, I got quiet and started to believe it.</p>
        <p>So I accepted a challenge — not to do more, but to finally see clearly what I was already doing. I grabbed a notebook from my nightstand and started writing down dates. Just the date, and a simple initial next to it. My own private shorthand.</p>
        <p>When I looked back at those pages, <strong>what I saw stopped me completely.</strong> I had been showing up all along. The proof was right there in my own handwriting.</p>
        <p><strong>Challenge accepted. And challenge met.</strong> That notebook became Tatum — because I knew I wasn't the only woman who needed to see this.</p>
